1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,160
It's not a dream, right?

2
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:06,420
This is the real you, right?

3
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:08,920
Of course it's me.

4
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:10,540
Thanks for waking me up.

5
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:13,280
And thank you too, Kuroi.

6
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:15,220
You're not hurt or anything, are you?

7
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,000
No, I'm okay.

8
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:18,460
What about you?

9
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:19,800
Are you feeling okay?

10
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:22,120
Show me your soul, Jim, and I can...

11
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:23,720
Would you stop worrying? I'm fine.

12
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:26,680
Look it, I'm better than ever, and it's all thanks to you.

13
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:29,520
Where are we?

14
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,660
I don't recognize this place.

15
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:35,680
We're in a rumor called the Eternal Sakura, I think.

16
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:37,340
The Eternal Sakura?

17
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:40,860
It's not in the rumor files I've seen.

18
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:44,340
It seems this tree is its core.

19
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,060
I think I've heard that name before.

20
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:51,260
Somewhere.

21
00:00:51,260 --> 00:01:01,640
Now what?

22
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:02,660
It's the Labyrinth!

23
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:07,960
I'll be waiting for you, Irohata Maki.

24
00:01:08,620 --> 00:01:13,240
I'll wait right here until the day you and the other three come to visit me.

25
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:17,460
I'll wait as long as it takes.

26
00:01:17,580 --> 00:01:21,240
Even if all the stories end, I'll be waiting.

27
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:27,580
It's the Alley, right where we entered.

28
00:01:28,580 --> 00:01:30,400
It seems that Uasa escaped.

29
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:31,700
It's the Labyrinth

30
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:32,160
It smells like that.

31
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:32,660
But...

32
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:38,040
The Universal cinema is not overwSo..

33
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:38,440
It's like us?

34
00:01:38,440 --> 00:01:38,920
It feels like nine o'clock would hurt.

35
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:39,040
It feels like the first one landed.

36
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:39,440
The Labyrinth has been الذ standing on o'clock and pressed..

37
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:39,740
It feels like everything at all.

38
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:40,500
It feels like us didn'tose the alarm.

39
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:41,240
I don't fall like you guys for the suit as we were a boy!

40
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:42,600
It feels like we're up at our team.

41
00:01:42,740 --> 00:01:45,520
It feels like you say Kadesi, so that The Lad garder is a sophomore.

42
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:46,340
So you can't 8th according to Doh, where the Lord importantly needs to get you down.

43
00:03:01,973 --> 00:03:05,793
We're home!

44
00:03:10,693 --> 00:03:14,513
It's usually way cleaner than this!

45
00:03:14,953 --> 00:03:16,993
Yachiyo's kind of a stickler about tidiness.

46
00:03:17,293 --> 00:03:17,653
Really?

47
00:03:18,873 --> 00:03:20,733
Yes, but I've been busy lately.

48
00:03:21,953 --> 00:03:23,573
Where are all the other girls?

49
00:03:24,993 --> 00:03:27,013
Yeah, Yachiyo. Where are they?

50
00:03:27,773 --> 00:03:29,013
I don't know.

51
00:03:29,013 --> 00:03:31,533
I saw them last at the Memory Museum.

52
00:03:32,493 --> 00:03:34,233
The Magius probably has them now.

53
00:03:34,433 --> 00:03:35,153
Oh no!

54
00:03:37,013 --> 00:03:40,493
How about you? You're a black feather. You must know something.

55
00:03:41,233 --> 00:03:44,693
If you're talking about the girls in Iroha's dream, I don't.

56
00:03:45,313 --> 00:03:47,993
I've never seen them around Magius' headquarters before.

57
00:03:48,793 --> 00:03:52,013
Hold on a second! You mean you're in the wings of the Magius?!

58
00:03:52,013 --> 00:03:53,613
Uh, yeah, sort of.

59
00:03:54,073 --> 00:03:56,193
She was sent to hunt you down, Iroha.

60
00:03:56,193 --> 00:03:59,833
By one of her leaders. A girl named Nemu Hiragi.

61
00:04:00,273 --> 00:04:01,333
No way! Really?

62
00:04:01,333 --> 00:04:06,473
I wasn't hunting you. Nemu wanted me to find you and bring you back to her is all.

63
00:04:07,173 --> 00:04:10,633
Wait, then you spoke to her? So is she doing okay? Is she?

64
00:04:10,833 --> 00:04:11,153
Uh...

65
00:04:11,153 --> 00:04:14,673
I haven't seen her in forever and I'm worried about her.

66
00:04:15,193 --> 00:04:16,713
I'm sorry, but...

67
00:04:16,713 --> 00:04:18,113
She told me she's dying.

68
00:04:18,113 --> 00:04:25,653
What are you talking about? Nemu's dying? For real? I-I'm sorry.

69
00:04:26,833 --> 00:04:31,833
Nemu is the one making all the rumors. As for Toka, she's the one who makes the doppels.

70
00:04:32,793 --> 00:04:36,993
You need to tell us what the Magius are planning. Does it have something to do with Nemu's condition?

71
00:04:36,993 --> 00:04:42,133
I really don't know anything. I just do what I'm told, that's all.

72
00:04:42,133 --> 00:04:46,533
All right, then. I believe you, but you have to take me to see them right away!

73
00:04:46,533 --> 00:04:53,153
We were all friends. The best of friends. We were always together and always had fun.

74
00:04:54,013 --> 00:04:58,453
I remember how sweet and cheerful they were. They were like my special little sisters.

75
00:04:59,913 --> 00:05:03,893
But when I saw Toka again, she didn't remember me at all.

76
00:05:03,893 --> 00:05:10,633
I think that if Nemu remembers me, maybe we can get some answers out of her.

77
00:05:10,973 --> 00:05:15,833
We can find out what the Magius are really up to. And maybe we can even save Nemu's life!

78
00:05:16,393 --> 00:05:17,373
I don't know.

79
00:05:18,133 --> 00:05:23,433
Iroha, I know how you must feel. But you hurt her. Nemu wanted to capture you.

80
00:05:23,733 --> 00:05:25,573
That's right, and I want to find out why.

81
00:05:25,573 --> 00:05:28,573
I don't know why I lost touch with her and Toka.

82
00:05:28,993 --> 00:05:31,673
Or what happened to my friends from the villa while I was asleep.

83
00:05:31,973 --> 00:05:33,153
Or why I was asleep.

84
00:05:33,893 --> 00:05:35,493
I can't just sit here and do nothing.

85
00:05:36,333 --> 00:05:37,973
All I want is to get some answers.

86
00:05:42,933 --> 00:05:43,713
All right, then.

87
00:05:44,633 --> 00:05:47,053
Let's go find our roommates and Nemu and Toka.

88
00:05:47,913 --> 00:05:48,273
Kuroi,

89
00:05:49,853 --> 00:05:53,153
take us to your HQ, to Hotel Fent Hope.

90
00:05:53,893 --> 00:05:54,353
Now.

91
00:05:58,353 --> 00:06:03,293
The massive typhoon that formed in the Southern Seas absorbed several other typhoons

92
00:06:03,293 --> 00:06:04,253
and is heading north.

93
00:06:04,253 --> 00:06:09,053
The weather bureau warns that it will reach landfall soon, so be prepared to evacuate.

94
00:06:09,053 --> 00:06:20,713
The thing about Hotel Fent Hope is it's constantly moving, so the door's always in a different spot.

95
00:06:20,713 --> 00:06:27,613
It looks like that trellis of Chinese cucumber is where the door is now.

96
00:06:28,113 --> 00:06:29,633
So how do we get inside?

97
00:06:30,353 --> 00:06:31,733
We have to use this thing.

98
00:06:35,393 --> 00:06:37,193
Wait, I didn't do that.

99
00:06:37,193 --> 00:06:43,373
The Omanes.

100
00:06:43,733 --> 00:06:44,413
Oh my gosh.

101
00:06:44,733 --> 00:06:46,573
What are you people doing here?

102
00:06:47,013 --> 00:06:49,233
Only members of Magia's know about the store.

103
00:06:49,933 --> 00:06:50,273
Aha!

104
00:06:50,633 --> 00:06:52,613
That Black Feather Rookie betrayed us!

105
00:06:53,053 --> 00:06:53,313
What?

106
00:06:53,573 --> 00:06:54,493
No, I didn't.

107
00:06:54,753 --> 00:06:57,153
One of the Magia's sent me out on a mission to bring...

108
00:06:57,153 --> 00:06:59,173
To bring Yachiyo Nanami in for a visit?

109
00:06:59,393 --> 00:07:00,733
I don't think so.

110
00:07:00,953 --> 00:07:02,013
He didn't have a choice.

111
00:07:04,313 --> 00:07:04,833
Hurry!

112
00:07:05,313 --> 00:07:05,913
Okay!

113
00:07:10,613 --> 00:07:11,913
That does it, Yachiyo.

114
00:07:12,053 --> 00:07:14,553
This is the last time you're going to interfere with us!

115
00:07:19,693 --> 00:07:23,353
We're going to get you back for all the times you stuck your nose in our plans.

116
00:07:24,033 --> 00:07:24,973
Come on, then.

117
00:07:27,153 --> 00:07:38,013
So this is Hotel Fent help.

118
00:07:38,853 --> 00:07:39,773
Yeah, sort of.

119
00:07:40,193 --> 00:07:42,473
We ended up in the basement level, actually.

120
00:07:42,813 --> 00:07:43,133
Really?

121
00:07:43,933 --> 00:07:47,213
Those white feathers we ran into must have exited through here.

122
00:07:49,213 --> 00:07:50,813
Can you hear me, Yachiyo?

123
00:07:51,813 --> 00:07:52,373
Yachiyo?

124
00:07:53,513 --> 00:07:55,333
Oh great, the portal's closed.

125
00:07:57,153 --> 00:07:58,853
I hope Yachiyo's okay.

126
00:08:00,793 --> 00:08:02,773
I'm sure she's doing just fine.

127
00:08:03,153 --> 00:08:04,473
She can handle those too.

128
00:08:04,893 --> 00:08:05,853
I hope so.

129
00:08:05,853 --> 00:08:12,793
Will this train take us to the main part of the hotel?

130
00:08:13,393 --> 00:08:14,773
It'll get us closer to it.

131
00:08:14,773 --> 00:08:20,633
Before you said, Nemu told you to come find me.

132
00:08:21,913 --> 00:08:22,333
Mm-hmm.

133
00:08:23,033 --> 00:08:24,173
Did she look sick?

134
00:08:24,873 --> 00:08:26,053
I couldn't tell.

135
00:08:26,433 --> 00:08:26,753
Oh.

136
00:08:26,753 --> 00:08:28,893
I'm curious.

137
00:08:28,893 --> 00:08:34,173
What made you decide to join the wings of the Magius?

138
00:08:34,173 --> 00:08:37,193
There weren't many witches left in my town.

139
00:08:37,653 --> 00:08:41,253
And when I came here for grief seeds, the witches were too strong for me.

140
00:08:41,253 --> 00:08:44,013
But you didn't have to join the Magius.

141
00:08:44,273 --> 00:08:46,153
Other magical girls would have helped you.

142
00:08:46,373 --> 00:08:46,973
Yeah, maybe.

143
00:08:47,513 --> 00:08:49,773
But I've used my doppel a bunch, so...

144
00:08:49,773 --> 00:08:50,053
What?

145
00:08:50,513 --> 00:08:51,633
That's bad for you!

146
00:08:52,013 --> 00:08:54,593
Yeah, but without it, I'd be a witch now.

147
00:08:55,773 --> 00:08:57,393
It's the same with you, isn't it?

148
00:08:57,393 --> 00:08:59,073
I guess so.

149
00:08:59,313 --> 00:09:01,653
But I almost lost control of my doppel.

150
00:09:01,953 --> 00:09:03,193
That was too close.

151
00:09:04,193 --> 00:09:05,933
Well, I say we stop using them.

152
00:09:06,333 --> 00:09:08,773
We don't need to rely on our doppels if we don't want to.

153
00:09:09,313 --> 00:09:11,853
If we all work together, we can do anything!

154
00:09:12,233 --> 00:09:14,133
I don't think it's as easy as all that.

155
00:09:14,693 --> 00:09:17,533
I'd feel terrible if someone ended up dying for my sake.

156
00:09:18,973 --> 00:09:21,373
All I'm saying is, you have friends now.

157
00:09:21,633 --> 00:09:23,313
You don't need the Magius' help.

158
00:09:24,693 --> 00:09:27,353
Anyway, you're not alone in this city.

159
00:09:28,033 --> 00:09:32,313
Hey, do you know if any other magical girls from Takarazaki came here before you?

160
00:09:38,993 --> 00:09:40,013
Are you okay?

161
00:09:41,113 --> 00:09:44,753
What would you do if all the magical girls that came to Kamehama

162
00:09:44,753 --> 00:09:47,953
came because they were so weak they couldn't survive on their own?

163
00:09:48,573 --> 00:09:50,393
That's easy. I'd help them out.

164
00:09:51,533 --> 00:09:53,553
Someone helped me when I needed it.

165
00:09:53,553 --> 00:10:10,593
I don't remember what's up ahead here, so be careful.

166
00:10:10,593 --> 00:10:17,893
It's Rana!

167
00:10:18,653 --> 00:10:19,133
Iroha!

168
00:10:19,513 --> 00:10:21,593
Where have you been? We were worried sick!

169
00:10:22,053 --> 00:10:23,093
Oh, um...

170
00:10:23,093 --> 00:10:24,473
I got stuck in something.

171
00:10:24,753 --> 00:10:26,393
I was worried about you guys, too.

172
00:10:26,713 --> 00:10:28,013
Does that cloak mean you...

173
00:10:28,013 --> 00:10:28,313
Yeah.

174
00:10:28,953 --> 00:10:30,453
I joined the wings of the Magius.

175
00:10:30,733 --> 00:10:31,653
I'm a black feather.

176
00:10:33,273 --> 00:10:34,713
At least I used to be.

177
00:10:34,953 --> 00:10:35,193
Huh?

178
00:10:35,193 --> 00:10:37,313
We ran out on them.

179
00:10:37,793 --> 00:10:38,413
It's safe!

180
00:10:42,753 --> 00:10:43,113
Kaire!

181
00:10:44,113 --> 00:10:45,653
What happened? Are you hurt?

182
00:10:46,293 --> 00:10:47,953
No, and her Soul Gem's fine, too.

183
00:10:48,253 --> 00:10:50,013
She's sick of this place and these people.

184
00:10:50,313 --> 00:10:52,173
She'll feel better once we get her out of here.

185
00:10:52,913 --> 00:10:55,693
On second thought, maybe we should go back.

186
00:10:55,813 --> 00:10:57,853
What? Have you lost your mind?

187
00:10:58,153 --> 00:10:59,873
I didn't come all this way just to...

188
00:10:59,873 --> 00:11:01,393
I don't feel right about this.

189
00:11:01,593 --> 00:11:04,553
If we went back and talked to everyone, that won't work.

190
00:11:05,333 --> 00:11:06,853
This is all my fault.

191
00:11:07,313 --> 00:11:10,093
I should have done what the coordinator said to do.

192
00:11:10,593 --> 00:11:11,113
Whatever.

193
00:11:11,633 --> 00:11:13,153
We're getting out. Come on.

194
00:11:13,153 --> 00:11:15,373
No! Wait!

195
00:11:16,073 --> 00:11:18,253
For what? We need to leave now.

196
00:11:19,013 --> 00:11:22,713
When we got to the entrance, the Amane sisters suddenly showed up.

197
00:11:23,073 --> 00:11:24,433
They closed the portal.

198
00:11:25,033 --> 00:11:26,373
There's white feathers up ahead?

199
00:11:26,713 --> 00:11:27,953
Why didn't you say so?

200
00:11:28,213 --> 00:11:29,213
That I just did!

201
00:11:30,073 --> 00:11:31,133
Sorry I snapped.

202
00:11:31,513 --> 00:11:32,993
But we can't stand around talking.

203
00:11:33,353 --> 00:11:34,133
We're being followed.

204
00:11:34,853 --> 00:11:37,873
We'll have to take the long way back to Fent Hope and find another way out.

205
00:11:38,193 --> 00:11:39,333
Do you know where you're going?

206
00:11:39,793 --> 00:11:40,973
Yeah, of course I do.

207
00:11:41,313 --> 00:11:42,113
Don't I, Kaire?

208
00:11:42,113 --> 00:11:43,273
Yeah.

209
00:11:44,193 --> 00:11:44,793
R-Rena!

210
00:11:45,173 --> 00:11:47,573
I think you should let a coordinator check her out.

211
00:11:47,833 --> 00:11:48,493
No way!

212
00:11:52,013 --> 00:11:52,993
Stay together.

213
00:11:58,113 --> 00:11:58,913
Huh?

214
00:11:58,913 --> 00:11:59,013
Huh?

215
00:12:12,113 --> 00:12:18,493
We keep hitting dead ends.

216
00:12:19,493 --> 00:12:22,193
The Magical Girls here won't tell us anything about the Magius.

217
00:12:23,013 --> 00:12:27,273
And none of the ones we talked to so far seem to know anything about Mommy either.

218
00:12:27,273 --> 00:12:32,013
By the look of these flyers, the Magius are actively recruiting Magical Girls.

219
00:12:32,333 --> 00:12:34,193
So why are they avoiding us?

220
00:12:34,553 --> 00:12:37,033
It's like banging our heads against a wall.

221
00:12:37,573 --> 00:12:38,313
I know.

222
00:12:38,533 --> 00:12:39,953
I hope Mommy's okay.

223
00:12:40,993 --> 00:12:41,933
We all do.

224
00:12:41,933 --> 00:12:49,653
At least we're not walking around in a cave anymore.

225
00:12:51,113 --> 00:12:52,213
Where are you going?

226
00:12:52,353 --> 00:12:52,813
Stop!

227
00:12:52,933 --> 00:12:53,413
Iroha?

228
00:12:53,413 --> 00:12:53,553
Huh?

229
00:12:53,553 --> 00:13:05,353
What is all this?

230
00:13:05,353 --> 00:13:08,913
No way!

231
00:13:09,133 --> 00:13:10,733
They're all filled with...

232
00:13:10,733 --> 00:13:11,413
Witches!

233
00:13:12,413 --> 00:13:14,393
This is where the Magius raise them.

234
00:13:14,813 --> 00:13:15,953
They can raise witches?

235
00:13:16,393 --> 00:13:16,793
Yeah.

236
00:13:17,213 --> 00:13:19,213
They call this place their witch farm.

237
00:13:19,933 --> 00:13:23,793
They catch a witch, bring it here, and raise it by feeding it human emotions.

238
00:13:23,793 --> 00:13:26,213
Is that what the rumors are for?

239
00:13:26,673 --> 00:13:29,173
To catch people so they can get food for witches?

240
00:13:29,913 --> 00:13:31,273
Yeah, that's how it works.

241
00:13:31,733 --> 00:13:33,073
Why would they do this?

242
00:13:33,373 --> 00:13:35,193
To get their gravestites, I guess.

243
00:13:35,793 --> 00:13:38,073
I mean, why else would they do something so crazy?

244
00:13:38,693 --> 00:13:39,413
That's cruel!

245
00:13:39,953 --> 00:13:43,893
Sure, they're witches now, but at one point they were magical girls like us!

246
00:13:44,213 --> 00:13:45,073
Yeah, I know.

247
00:13:45,493 --> 00:13:48,073
It sucks, but we need to focus on getting out.

248
00:13:49,213 --> 00:13:50,553
Doesn't that scare you?

249
00:13:50,933 --> 00:13:51,853
Ending up like them?

250
00:13:52,473 --> 00:13:52,893
No.

251
00:13:52,893 --> 00:13:54,413
Not even a little?

252
00:13:55,153 --> 00:13:56,453
It makes me sad.

253
00:13:56,713 --> 00:13:58,153
No one deserves this fate.

254
00:14:00,013 --> 00:14:05,373
To become a witch, then get locked up in a cage and forced to wait to be turned into a grief seat?

255
00:14:05,673 --> 00:14:06,873
It's not right!

256
00:14:08,093 --> 00:14:10,053
I can't imagine how that feels.

257
00:14:12,053 --> 00:14:15,273
What is that?

258
00:14:15,873 --> 00:14:16,933
It's not a witch!

259
00:14:17,373 --> 00:14:18,133
It's an Uasa!

260
00:14:18,873 --> 00:14:19,073
Shh!

261
00:14:19,273 --> 00:14:19,793
Watch out!

262
00:14:20,413 --> 00:14:21,513
This was a guard!

263
00:14:23,333 --> 00:14:27,793
I felt like

